    "items": [
     {
      "pClass": "productdescription",
      "pText": "Five coloured discs hang on chains from a steel frame, just above the ground, and the Disc Challenger asks children to cross from one to the next without stepping down. Each disc swings as it takes weight, so children hold the chains, shift their feet and plan the next step before they make it. It is a short challenge course in a footprint of 6'6\" x 3', with a safe play area of 11'6\" x 8', so it fits into a gap on an existing playground. Teachers can use it for turn-taking games and simple races. Colour is listed as Multi Color. The 3-year warranty on this unit covers galvanised pipe, roto-moulded parts, composite laminates and play rope. We can show it on your layout drawing."
     }
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "component": "ProductSpecifications2",
   "props": {
    "pText": "The hanging discs swing all the time, so their chains and top fixings need checking at every maintenance visit, with worn parts replaced promptly. The steel frame is grouted or installed self-standing. Lay rubber flooring under the discs and keep the 11'6\" x 8' zone clear, as the discs swing outward when children step off.",
